<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Who dares to bind by his dull sense</l><l>The oracles of heaven,</l><l>For all the nations, tongues and climes</l><l>And all the ages given!</l><l>The universe how much unknown!</l><l>That ocean unexplored!</l><l>The Lord hath yet more light and truth</l><l>To break forth from His Word.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Darkling our great forefathers went</l><l>The first steps of the way;</l><l>’Twas but the dawning yet to grow</l><l>Into the perfect day;</l><l>And grow it shall, our glorious Sun</l><l>More fervid rays afford:</l><l>The Lord hath yet more light and truth</l><l>To break forth from His Word.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>The valleys past, ascending still,</l><l>Our souls would higher climb,</l><l>And look down from supernal heights,</l><l>On all the bygone times;</l><l>Upward we press, the air is clear,</l><l>And the sphere-music heard!</l><l>The Lord hath yet more light and truth</l><l>To break forth from His Word.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>O Father, Son and Spirit, send</l><l>Us increase from above;</l><l>Enlarge, expand all Christian hearts</l><l>To comprehend Thy love;</l><l>And make us all go on to know</l><l>With nobler powers conferred:</l><l>The Lord hath yet more light and truth</l><l>To break forth from His Word.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
